WEBVTT

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:16.340
Mimi, bring some water.

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:17.360
Yes.

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:37.460
Vodka means water in Russian.

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:43.050
Maeno is tired of seeing this.

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:46.540
Kouki, if you're bored, go look for work or something.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:51.160
Hey, hey, I took care of that big mountain just yesterday.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:53.400
Thanks to that, my head hurts.

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:56.690
I'm sorry.

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:57.520
That time, I...

00:02:57.890 --> 00:03:01.170
No, that was my fault.

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:03.770
I should've left it to you.

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:06.370
I feel better because you said that.

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:10.830
This is Asougi Consulting.

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:14.160
Yes...

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:14.940
Yes.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:17.710
Rin. It's for you.

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:36.680
Asougi.

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:37.220
Rin-san.

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:39.280
You are?

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:42.910
I must tell you.

00:03:48.190 --> 00:03:49.330
What's wrong?

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:50.120
Are you okay?

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:03.340
Tokyo...

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:06.420
The flower of death will bloom in Tokyo!

00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:29.330
I found out who the girl is.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:32.460
Her name is Takimoto Yuria.

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:33.330
17 years old.

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:35.790
She commutes to a girls high school in the city,

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:37.930
a normal high school student.

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:40.230
She went missing a week ago,

00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:41.840
and her family has requested a search.

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:45.720
She'd be about the right age to be your daughter.

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:47.850
Why did someone like that call us?

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:50.790
This girl...

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:54.050
wanted to tell me something...

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:01.180
I feel bad about her dying right in front of me.

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:11.390
I was already an old man when I became part of this world.

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:16.460
But Mary kept saying I was beautiful.

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:18.530
So she was an old acquaintance of yours?

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:22.650
I heard she got dragged into this world during the war.

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:26.500
Because the lieutenant she reported to was a nice guy.

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:28.260
During the war, you say.

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:29.540
She must be pretty old.

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:33.150
She's probably more than 80 years old.

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:35.480
Then, she must've died of natural causes.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:37.850
It's not like that!

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:41.470
She died after getting involved with all those explosions!

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:53.430
You know, you shouldn't ask me for this kind of help so thoughtlessly.

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:55.700
I'm the chief detective, despite my appearance.

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:57.320
Assistant chief detective, right?

00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:02.140
I looked up that dead person.

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:03.340
Yuria-chan?

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:06.650
Cause of death was impact from the fall,

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:08.940
but she would've died anyway in her condition.

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:09.830
She was sick after all?

00:06:11.150 --> 00:06:13.340
Her lungs and brain were badly damaged.

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:14.640
What was the illness?

00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:16.510
Still unknown.

00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:17.410
Also...

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:23.640
She acted like a normal student,

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:26.390
but she was quite a pervert.

00:06:29.230 --> 00:06:31.120
It's unusual for you to frown.

00:06:31.650 --> 00:06:34.350
I just remembered something.

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:36.180
But it's impossible.

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:37.220
Huh?

00:06:37.220 --> 00:06:40.140
You said the same thing as that old doctor, the coroner.

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:40.700
What?

00:06:41.320 --> 00:06:43.810
I said that her illness is unknown, right?

00:06:43.810 --> 00:06:47.390
The doctor seemed to know about some similar illness.

00:06:47.390 --> 00:06:50.210
But just like you did now, he said it's impossible.

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:55.900
Genta, stop that!

00:06:57.360 --> 00:06:59.380
Okay! Okay, okay, okay!

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:01.930
Mimi, look this up.

00:07:01.930 --> 00:07:03.400
Shimizu Yoshie.

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:05.650
She should be in a nursing home.

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:07.560
Patient data?

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:10.390
Personal information is protected.

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:13.150
That's why I asked you.

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:15.510
I'll take you out to the pool.

00:07:15.510 --> 00:07:18.160
I'm not a child.

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:23.630
Yes.

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:28.870
You are...

00:07:29.690 --> 00:07:31.370
The granddaughter of Asougi Rin.

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:35.880
Where is Rin? Is she alive?

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:38.380
No, she's dead.

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:41.490
Dead?

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:43.280
That Rin?

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:45.390
Died before I did?

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:48.230
Sorry for surprising you.

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:50.390
You are Shimizu Yoshie-san, right?

00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:51.980
Yes.

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:54.490
There's something I wanted to ask you.

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:56.470
Something that happened during the war.

00:07:56.470 --> 00:07:58.020
I've forgotten.

00:07:58.020 --> 00:07:59.020
Go back.

00:07:59.890 --> 00:08:02.010
I don't want to talk about anything.

00:08:02.010 --> 00:08:02.900
Shimizu-san.

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:11.840
Rin is...

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:13.930
Did Rin say something like that?

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:21.310
Behind you, in the bottom drawer.

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:24.810
Everything is there.

00:08:35.150 --> 00:08:36.970
Showa 20 (1945).

00:08:36.970 --> 00:08:40.980
As commanded, I went to an isolated island, Shibitojima.

00:08:42.560 --> 00:08:46.990
I went to study Higan-byou, a disease that's local to Shibitojima.

00:08:50.870 --> 00:08:53.070
Flowers... Flowers are blooming.

00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:55.580
The flowers of hell!

00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:59.190
Early symptoms are similar to the flu.

00:08:59.190 --> 00:09:03.050
Fever, cough, and hiccups continue for a week.

00:09:03.580 --> 00:09:06.330
After that, the hands and feet begin to swell,

00:09:06.330 --> 00:09:09.280
and eventually the joints begin to hurt.

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:12.830
At that time, amnesia and hallucinations begin to worsen,

00:09:12.830 --> 00:09:15.810
and patients fall into a state of delirium.

00:09:16.350 --> 00:09:18.270
A common symptom is that

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:23.570
the patients say they see a red flower blooming.

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:27.040
Blood spots start to appear all over their bodies like flowers,

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:30.070
and this is the origin of the name Higan-byou.

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:34.790
Also, because the illness is fatal, the disease is called a way to go to the afterlife.

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:38.500
Because the risk of infection is very low,

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:42.190
the number of patients who contracted this disease while we were there...

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:45.710
was just one.

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:53.420
In other words, this was a biological weapon that the military was researching?

00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:54.420
Yes.

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:56.850
I can imagine what happened after this.

00:09:56.850 --> 00:10:00.760
After the loss of the war, the military ordered the destruction of all records.

00:10:00.760 --> 00:10:02.730
They placed a gag order on everyone involved.

00:10:04.340 --> 00:10:05.980
During that time,

00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:07.740
everything was in a state of confusion.

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:08.660
I didn't do anything!

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:09.330
Stop!

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:11.840
At the black market,

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:14.760
Yoshie was violating military orders by trying to sell goods illegally,

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:18.020
and I saved her from getting into trouble with the local authorities.

00:10:18.020 --> 00:10:22.260
At that time, she told me about this terrible sickness.

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:27.070
The symptoms are the same as Takimoto Yuria's, the person who died at the construction site?

00:10:27.070 --> 00:10:28.180
Yes.

00:10:28.180 --> 00:10:30.360
Then why didn't you say so earlier?

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:32.300
Because it's an impossible illness.

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:33.300
It's extinct?

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:35.960
That island is completely gone.

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:36.360
Eh?

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:39.530
After the war, all residents of Higashimejima,

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:41.670
commonly known as Shibitojima, were moved to the main islands,

00:10:41.670 --> 00:10:44.710
by order of the Self-Defense Force.

00:10:44.710 --> 00:10:49.320
After that, the island was destroyed by the eruption at Myoujinshou and underground earthquakes.

00:10:49.970 --> 00:10:53.030
The island was wiped off the face of the earth.

00:10:53.030 --> 00:10:56.080
Encountering a local disease from there seems quite impossible, right?

00:10:56.790 --> 00:10:59.410
But you confirmed it.

00:10:59.410 --> 00:11:01.650
Look for people who came from Shibitojima.

00:11:01.650 --> 00:11:04.180
But that was more than 60 years ago, right?

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:06.090
Even if they're still alive, they'll all be old.

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:07.590
Even so.

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:10.110
I understand.

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:14.390
Yes, this is Maeno.

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:18.750
Youko-san?

00:11:19.640 --> 00:11:21.580
No, I didn't forget.

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:24.630
I'm just surprised that you know this number.

00:11:28.010 --> 00:11:29.360
What did you say?

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:30.710
Todoroki has gone missing?

00:11:38.790 --> 00:11:41.830
Birds were everything to him.

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:46.350
You two knew each other since your university years, right?

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:48.060
You're kidding, right?

00:11:48.710 --> 00:11:51.300
No, it's in our manuals to confirm such things.

00:11:52.860 --> 00:11:56.020
Even though you made fun of the manuals during your university years...

00:11:57.340 --> 00:11:59.060
It's just that I've became an adult.

00:12:00.620 --> 00:12:03.520
Todoroki never could become an adult.

00:12:04.330 --> 00:12:07.580
If only he'd outgrown birds, he could've been happy.

00:12:08.340 --> 00:12:10.260
How long has he been missing?

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:11.710
For a week.

00:12:12.380 --> 00:12:15.600
He called to say he'd be coming back as usual.

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:16.900
And since then...

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:19.150
Were there any warning signs or something like that?

00:12:20.520 --> 00:12:21.160
Just that...

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:24.660
after he was gone, when I took a look at his desk,

00:12:25.650 --> 00:12:26.600
I found this.

00:12:46.060 --> 00:12:47.480
All right!

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:50.970
Listen to this. The second one went up.

00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:53.100
The first one is Shinkoutetsu.

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:55.490
They specialize in making nozzles.

00:12:56.780 --> 00:12:58.430
We're having a warm winter this year, right?

00:12:58.430 --> 00:13:02.760
Shinkoutetsu has a 60% market share in the snow-making machine business.

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:07.440
The other one is Tenmon, an IT security company.

00:13:07.440 --> 00:13:10.490
They've developed new security systems for the net.

00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:12.250
That makes them your natural enemy, right?

00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:15.980
Since I've become a shareholder, I've been able to get more information.

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:19.450
They wouldn't think that a shareholder is a hacker as well.

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:22.270
And? Where are the residents of Shibitojima?

00:13:22.270 --> 00:13:23.610
Okay, okay.

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:27.770
When you find something, contact Maeno.

00:13:30.430 --> 00:13:31.540
Geez.

00:13:33.320 --> 00:13:34.800
I was thinking just now.

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:37.800
Make a list of all the victims from those explosions too.

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:38.720
Why?

00:13:38.720 --> 00:13:39.740
They aren't related, are they?

00:13:40.270 --> 00:13:43.420
I'm wondering if former military personnel are involved.

00:13:46.180 --> 00:13:49.010
You said this was a reward for finding Shimizu Yoshie.

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:51.100
But you just wanted to swim, right?

00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:53.860
Speaking of that, not too long ago,

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:56.590
he said he saw some strange men.

00:13:57.060 --> 00:13:58.540
Strange men?

00:13:58.540 --> 00:13:59.320
Yes.

00:13:59.320 --> 00:14:01.210
On the nesting grounds of the oystercatchers.

00:14:01.210 --> 00:14:03.850
I believe it was at Sanbanze.

00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:13.880
Yes.

00:14:13.880 --> 00:14:14.740
It's me.

00:14:14.740 --> 00:14:17.090
I found the list of residents at Shibitojima.

00:14:17.090 --> 00:14:20.180
It's an old source, so I don't think it will help much.

00:14:20.180 --> 00:14:21.450
I'll send it to you by email.

00:14:22.340 --> 00:14:24.480
Rin will help too, right?

00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:26.980
She's busy with those explosions.

00:14:27.580 --> 00:14:28.470
What's happening?

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:33.580
It was just as you said.

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:34.460
Is that right?

00:14:34.710 --> 00:14:36.820
Either they were just passing through,

00:14:36.820 --> 00:14:38.970
or they just happened to be there.

00:14:39.570 --> 00:14:42.850
So I don't think the old man was a target.

00:14:42.850 --> 00:14:45.290
Hiding a tree in a forest.

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:48.180
Hiding a corpse among corpses?

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:49.480
Give me a break.

00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:53.480
How many people do you think died in these incidents?

00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:56.980
Let's just hope that this isn't a precursor of things to come.

00:14:57.470 --> 00:15:02.020
Hey, during the war, former military medical staff personnel...

00:15:02.620 --> 00:15:04.930
What are you sticking your nose into this time?

00:15:04.930 --> 00:15:06.180
I wonder?

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:09.000
I don't really know.

00:15:12.200 --> 00:15:13.710
It's nothing.

00:15:39.110 --> 00:15:40.660
Will you let me eat it?

00:15:41.280 --> 00:15:42.720
Your memories.

00:15:44.410 --> 00:15:45.510
I've heard.

00:15:45.510 --> 00:15:47.500
Jane disappeared.

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:49.900
I didn't think she was a stripper.

00:15:50.710 --> 00:15:53.190
Yes, angels again?

00:15:53.190 --> 00:15:54.050
Or could it be...

00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:56.170
Eh?

00:15:57.230 --> 00:15:59.170
I have. Angels.

00:16:00.010 --> 00:16:05.760
You can't. You always ask for things I don't have.

00:16:07.670 --> 00:16:10.260
There are things that would surprise even you.

00:16:10.260 --> 00:16:12.610
It's okay. Don't worry.

00:16:13.090 --> 00:16:15.140
It's in the hands of trustworthy people.

00:16:23.820 --> 00:16:25.220
I'm happy.

00:16:25.220 --> 00:16:27.270
Hot pots are the best on cold days.

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:29.120
Where's Teruki?

00:16:29.120 --> 00:16:32.290
He said he'd stay awake until you came back, but...

00:16:32.610 --> 00:16:36.270
It's okay. It's best for kids to sleep early and wake up early.

00:16:36.270 --> 00:16:37.440
Now then...

00:16:37.440 --> 00:16:39.040
Thanks for the meal.

00:16:40.170 --> 00:16:41.410
I-It's hot.

00:16:41.950 --> 00:16:44.050
Geez, don't rush.

00:16:55.710 --> 00:16:56.460
Hello.

00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:00.540
What did you say?

00:17:02.920 --> 00:17:03.760
Where's Rin?

00:17:09.280 --> 00:17:10.310
Damn it.

00:17:10.310 --> 00:17:12.140
What's their purpose in taking Rin?

00:17:12.140 --> 00:17:14.310
They're after the Shibitojima records.

00:17:15.280 --> 00:17:17.330
Our office is in a terrible state too.

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:18.830
Then, Rin is...

00:17:19.340 --> 00:17:20.700
I don't know.

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:22.170
I can't contact her at all.

00:17:24.280 --> 00:17:25.130
Rin.

00:17:26.280 --> 00:17:27.730
Where are you?

00:17:35.800 --> 00:17:37.530
Ow...

00:17:43.150 --> 00:17:44.110
9mm?

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:52.740
This smell of rotten fruit...

00:18:26.150 --> 00:18:27.840
Don't worry.

00:18:27.840 --> 00:18:30.600
Things like this have happened many times before, right?

00:18:30.600 --> 00:18:32.150
It's different from usual.

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:34.580
I've had premonitions about that.

00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:39.400
I was wondering if a day like this would come eventually.

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:42.800
When Rin would stick her nose too deep into trouble.

00:18:43.370 --> 00:18:46.660
You're not anxious just because you're immortal.

00:18:46.660 --> 00:18:48.750
So why?

00:18:48.750 --> 00:18:50.950
Why do you do dangerous jobs like this?

00:18:51.440 --> 00:18:54.190
You should've just lived quietly instead of doing something like this.

00:18:56.480 --> 00:18:59.730
Living doesn't just mean not dying.

00:19:00.530 --> 00:19:02.350
It's the same for you.

00:19:02.350 --> 00:19:04.960
If your livelihood was guaranteed from now on,

00:19:04.960 --> 00:19:06.400
would you go on living without doing anything?

00:19:07.400 --> 00:19:08.900
If I could stay with my family.

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:10.150
That's a lie.

00:19:12.870 --> 00:19:16.170
Men always want proof that they're alive.

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:19.920
Even if it means doing criminal acts that others frown on.

00:19:19.920 --> 00:19:21.970
They can't go on living without doing something.

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:27.190
For Rin and me, that just happens to mean the current job.

00:19:28.340 --> 00:19:31.410
We might be bored in another hundred years,

00:19:31.410 --> 00:19:35.460
but right now, doing this means being alive to us.

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:41.460
Where are you going?

00:19:41.460 --> 00:19:44.060
I'm going to look up the survivors of Shibitojima.

00:19:44.550 --> 00:19:46.840
That's about all I can do.

00:19:46.840 --> 00:19:47.890
That's right.

00:19:48.520 --> 00:19:51.170
Now is the time to do what we can.

00:19:51.780 --> 00:19:52.730
Todoroki.

00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:54.380
I'm sorry.

00:20:01.700 --> 00:20:02.550
Excuse me...

00:20:03.180 --> 00:20:05.230
You are Kitai Masagorou-san, right?

00:20:06.070 --> 00:20:07.040
From Higashimejima.

00:20:07.660 --> 00:20:08.780
Do you know about it?

00:20:08.780 --> 00:20:09.980
Higashimejima.

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:11.520
Or Shibitojima.

00:20:13.260 --> 00:20:15.440
The food isn't ready yet?

00:20:22.310 --> 00:20:24.880
Especially this one, Thousand Feet...

00:20:24.880 --> 00:20:28.510
Then, can I ask you about Higan-byou?

00:20:28.510 --> 00:20:30.800
It's a disease that's unique to Shibitojima.

00:20:32.340 --> 00:20:32.740
That's...

00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:39.130
If the One Eye stared at you, you'd get Higan-byou.

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:52.560
Kitai-san! Are you okay?

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:53.670
Kitai-san!

00:20:54.800 --> 00:20:55.690
Wait!

00:20:58.610 --> 00:21:00.430
The old man was the target?

00:21:15.110 --> 00:21:16.160
Kitai-san!

00:21:16.870 --> 00:21:19.170
I couldn't get more out of him.

00:21:19.530 --> 00:21:24.130
So then? The tattoo was the same as the one drawn by other Shibitojima residents.

00:21:24.440 --> 00:21:27.770
Moreover, Todoroki also drew the same thing.

00:21:27.770 --> 00:21:30.330
I wonder if those guys took Rin away?

00:21:30.330 --> 00:21:32.280
There's a good chance of that.

00:21:36.020 --> 00:21:38.120
I don't like it, but I guess I have to ask her.

00:21:46.360 --> 00:21:49.550
Don't judge people by their appearance!

00:21:49.550 --> 00:21:51.410
Endure it.

00:21:51.410 --> 00:21:53.410
We didn't come here to play.

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:55.630
Even I'm having this. Look, ginger ale.

00:21:55.630 --> 00:21:57.180
Of course.

00:21:57.180 --> 00:21:58.960
A grasshopper.

00:22:01.480 --> 00:22:03.760
You're still small, aren't you?

00:22:03.760 --> 00:22:05.310
Leave me alone.

00:22:05.310 --> 00:22:07.270
First time I've seen this guy.

00:22:07.270 --> 00:22:08.420
Nice to meet you.

00:22:09.050 --> 00:22:09.920
Nice to meet you.

00:22:10.930 --> 00:22:12.680
Let's get straight to business.

00:22:12.680 --> 00:22:14.030
Before that.

00:22:14.030 --> 00:22:17.800
You know that I won't act just for money, right?

00:22:19.770 --> 00:22:21.010
No!

00:22:21.010 --> 00:22:21.720
Never.

00:22:22.520 --> 00:22:24.190
You're worried about Rin, right?

00:22:27.370 --> 00:22:28.320
Mimi?

00:22:41.360 --> 00:22:43.010
Look.

00:22:43.010 --> 00:22:45.750
Look, and don't touch.

00:22:45.750 --> 00:22:47.450
That was the deal, right?

00:22:49.050 --> 00:22:50.480
Don't look.

00:22:52.840 --> 00:22:53.890
Is it okay?

00:22:53.890 --> 00:22:58.060
If you don't look, what she's doing will go to waste.

00:23:14.180 --> 00:23:15.790
We kept our end of the deal.

00:23:16.240 --> 00:23:18.150
It's to protect Rin.

00:23:18.150 --> 00:23:18.980
Now.

00:23:18.980 --> 00:23:20.040
I know.

00:23:21.220 --> 00:23:22.250
This is Kudal.

00:23:22.850 --> 00:23:23.550
Kudal?

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:26.350
More accurately, evil sight in Sanskrit.

00:23:26.350 --> 00:23:28.510
Kudal means Evil Eye.

00:23:28.940 --> 00:23:30.620
If you're seen by that eye,

00:23:30.620 --> 00:23:33.390
you will experience great misfortune.

00:23:33.780 --> 00:23:34.770
That's right.

00:23:34.770 --> 00:23:36.480
In the past,

00:23:36.480 --> 00:23:39.070
when a man contracted a disease that couldn't be explained,

00:23:39.070 --> 00:23:41.920
he was said to be a victim of the Evil Eye.

00:23:42.690 --> 00:23:46.450
Kudal has been very active in the underworld recently.

00:23:46.450 --> 00:23:48.450
Most of their deals are about arms.

00:23:48.450 --> 00:23:50.500
They're quite a cult.

00:23:50.500 --> 00:23:52.780
I don't really want to get involved.

00:23:52.780 --> 00:23:54.240
There are people like them in Tokyo?

00:23:55.000 --> 00:23:58.210
Japan is a fertile field for those kinds of things.

00:23:58.210 --> 00:24:00.470
That's why all commerce happens here.

00:24:00.470 --> 00:24:01.440
How is Rin related to this?

00:24:01.860 --> 00:24:03.440
I wonder?

00:24:03.440 --> 00:24:06.170
I can investigate for you.

00:24:06.170 --> 00:24:08.920
Of course, it'll be expensive.

00:24:10.350 --> 00:24:13.350
There's no need to pay any more to that woman.

00:24:13.350 --> 00:24:15.110
I've heard about Kudal.

00:24:15.110 --> 00:24:17.010
I know where I can get more information too.

00:24:17.740 --> 00:24:18.840
What are you going to do?

00:24:19.400 --> 00:24:21.300
I'm going to break into the Special Ops Second Division.

00:24:21.820 --> 00:24:23.090
Can you do something like that?

00:24:23.900 --> 00:24:28.400
The Second Division recently installed Tenmon's security system.

00:24:29.640 --> 00:24:33.990
Also, even if it's the CIA or MI6, I can break in.

00:24:33.990 --> 00:24:35.090
If it's for Rin.

00:24:49.610 --> 00:24:50.810
As I thought.

00:24:51.970 --> 00:24:53.380
You're alive.

00:24:53.380 --> 00:24:54.250
Well.

00:25:04.950 --> 00:25:07.230
I thought I was saved.

00:25:08.640 --> 00:25:10.540
But staying alive was hell.

00:25:13.170 --> 00:25:16.120
Thanks to medical technology, I'm able to move around like this.

00:25:16.730 --> 00:25:19.100
I've waited 20 years for this development.

00:25:19.630 --> 00:25:21.080
It's mysterious.

00:25:21.640 --> 00:25:25.990
The Fruit of Immortality recreates forever the form you had when it entered your body.

00:25:26.620 --> 00:25:29.250
If you're healthy, you're healthy forever.

00:25:29.250 --> 00:25:30.800
If you're sick, you're sick forever.

00:25:31.580 --> 00:25:33.120
Why do you think that is?

00:25:33.870 --> 00:25:36.800
In the first place, what is Yggdrasill?

00:25:37.740 --> 00:25:40.610
Why can only immortals see it?

00:25:40.610 --> 00:25:43.360
Why can Fruits of Immortality that pass through people's bodies

00:25:43.360 --> 00:25:46.390
be seen by normal humans?

00:25:46.390 --> 00:25:48.370
Why do only females become immortal,

00:25:48.370 --> 00:25:50.650
and males become angels?

00:25:50.650 --> 00:25:51.550
Do you know?

00:25:53.280 --> 00:25:55.680
I don't know.

00:25:55.680 --> 00:25:57.980
That's why I'm going to experiment on you.

00:25:57.980 --> 00:25:59.330
Experiment?

00:26:00.440 --> 00:26:02.700
I thought it was some new way of playing.

00:26:03.510 --> 00:26:05.600
That's true too.

00:26:05.600 --> 00:26:09.610
I wonder how often I can destroy you before you're unable to regenerate?

00:26:09.610 --> 00:26:12.420
Even if I take out all of your organs?

00:26:12.420 --> 00:26:13.740
Even if I leave just your head?

00:26:16.040 --> 00:26:17.840
Let me ask you one thing.

00:26:19.090 --> 00:26:21.040
Why did Yuria-chan die?

00:26:21.640 --> 00:26:22.380
Yuria?

00:26:23.180 --> 00:26:24.170
Ah, that girl.

00:26:25.220 --> 00:26:27.940
She died because she was an idiot, of course.

00:26:27.940 --> 00:26:30.140
Even though I played with her in various ways.

00:26:31.710 --> 00:26:34.500
Even though I took her to Tokyo on business.

00:26:34.500 --> 00:26:36.030
She ran away on her own.

00:26:36.840 --> 00:26:39.080
Why did she come to me?

00:26:39.080 --> 00:26:40.830
I wonder?

00:26:40.830 --> 00:26:44.200
Probably because I mentioned your name when I was torturing her.

00:26:44.200 --> 00:26:46.450
Maybe she thought you could save her.

00:26:47.880 --> 00:26:51.680
I was surprised when she went to you for help.

00:26:51.680 --> 00:26:55.760
But I didn't think you'd know Shimizu Yoshie.

00:26:55.760 --> 00:26:57.580
You never grew older.

00:26:58.320 --> 00:27:02.100
Well, both of us have lots of time.

00:27:03.060 --> 00:27:04.140
Enjoy.

00:27:07.220 --> 00:27:08.770
Do you hate me?

00:27:09.710 --> 00:27:12.710
No, I want you to hate me.

00:27:14.570 --> 00:27:17.060
As you suffer and feel pain,

00:27:17.060 --> 00:27:20.860
the taste that is imbued with hatred is the best.

00:27:24.430 --> 00:27:26.370
I'm going out for a bit.

00:27:27.220 --> 00:27:29.370
Stay here and relax.

00:28:09.750 --> 00:28:12.370
I hope you execute your plan soon.

00:28:12.790 --> 00:28:14.840
It seems a bit interesting.

00:28:18.950 --> 00:28:20.450
Also, that Rin.

00:28:20.450 --> 00:28:22.750
Don't despise her too much.

00:28:39.510 --> 00:28:40.510
Injection for anesthesia...

00:28:44.770 --> 00:28:48.660
You should check the medical equipment carefully.

00:28:48.660 --> 00:28:52.120
Sometimes things get left inside the patient's body.

00:29:06.980 --> 00:29:07.960
Damn you...

00:29:09.210 --> 00:29:10.360
You...

00:29:16.670 --> 00:29:18.150
N-No...

00:29:33.790 --> 00:29:35.290
The presence of an angel?

00:29:36.800 --> 00:29:37.900
It disappeared.

00:29:51.870 --> 00:29:53.850
What is this heat wave?

00:29:58.610 --> 00:30:01.800
The season changed while I was asleep?

00:30:02.850 --> 00:30:04.050
This is...

00:30:04.050 --> 00:30:05.030
Shibitojima?

00:30:05.660 --> 00:30:07.620
But that sank, didn't it?

00:30:07.620 --> 00:30:10.270
I finished analyzing the data in the Second Division.

00:30:10.270 --> 00:30:13.240
They're not fools either, so they know about Kudal's movements.

00:30:14.230 --> 00:30:16.550
This ship, which they believe belongs to Kudal,

00:30:16.550 --> 00:30:19.390
entered harbor on the day Takimoto Yuria died,

00:30:19.390 --> 00:30:22.250
and left harbor on the day Rin went missing.

00:30:22.890 --> 00:30:24.140
Do you think that's a coincidence?

00:30:24.140 --> 00:30:25.680
But because of that...

00:30:25.680 --> 00:30:27.700
Just to be sure, I searched a bit.

00:30:27.700 --> 00:30:28.260
Look at this.

00:30:29.120 --> 00:30:31.020
The area where Shibitojima was.

00:30:31.020 --> 00:30:32.690
There are no islands.

00:30:32.690 --> 00:30:34.140
To an amateur's eyes.

00:30:34.770 --> 00:30:37.140
They doctored the image.

00:30:37.610 --> 00:30:40.170
Then Shibitojima exists even now?

00:30:43.180 --> 00:30:44.400
This is Shibitojima.

00:30:45.250 --> 00:30:48.280
Why do you think the military evacuated all the residents?

00:30:48.280 --> 00:30:52.250
Because it's too far from the main islands, it has no strategic importance at all.

00:30:52.250 --> 00:30:54.830
It's the same as what the Japanese army tried to do, right?

00:30:55.090 --> 00:30:56.170
That's right.

00:30:56.170 --> 00:30:59.180
In an era when there's no perfect way to hide anything,

00:30:59.180 --> 00:31:01.460
if they want to develop biological weapons,

00:31:01.460 --> 00:31:03.920
they need to do it in the middle of a desert.

00:31:04.880 --> 00:31:08.240
The American Army has a base here for biological weapons.

00:31:08.240 --> 00:31:12.160
And the Japanese government accepted that.

00:31:12.160 --> 00:31:14.350
That's why this island disappeared from the map.

00:31:15.580 --> 00:31:16.520
Moreover,

00:31:16.520 --> 00:31:19.000
to protect that disappearance, they even circulated strange rumors

00:31:19.000 --> 00:31:22.180
about this island being destroyed by Myoujinshou's crustal movements.

00:31:23.500 --> 00:31:26.100
You... what are you after?

00:31:26.100 --> 00:31:27.490
A paradise for the immortal.

00:31:48.930 --> 00:31:49.630
See you.

00:31:50.900 --> 00:31:52.070
I'm going.

00:31:52.070 --> 00:31:54.970
I don't know when I'll return.

00:31:55.470 --> 00:31:58.510
Teruki, while I'm gone,

00:31:58.510 --> 00:31:59.600
take care of Mom.

00:32:00.250 --> 00:32:00.810
Yes.

00:32:03.120 --> 00:32:04.590
That's a good boy.

00:32:11.710 --> 00:32:13.100
You are...

00:32:13.100 --> 00:32:15.100
I received special payment.

00:32:18.460 --> 00:32:19.360
Mimi.

00:32:29.380 --> 00:32:31.630
Do you know about domoic acid?

00:32:31.630 --> 00:32:32.710
No, I don't.

00:32:32.710 --> 00:32:34.500
You should've studied more.

00:32:36.360 --> 00:32:38.700
The Japanese discovered it.

00:32:38.700 --> 00:32:41.200
It comes from red algae called Hanayagi.

00:32:47.980 --> 00:32:50.870
If you ingest a lot of domoic acid,

00:32:50.870 --> 00:32:54.170
the part of the brain that controls memory, the hippocampus, will be damaged.

00:32:55.090 --> 00:32:59.210
It bonds with large amounts of L-glutamine in the hippocampus.

00:32:59.210 --> 00:33:05.360
And the Higan-byou virus is made with an amino acid similar to domoic acid.

00:33:05.750 --> 00:33:08.490
However, the bonding strength is several orders of magnitude greater.

00:33:13.070 --> 00:33:17.840
Then the Higan-byou virus starts to eat the brain itself.

00:33:17.840 --> 00:33:20.850
Eventually, the host dies.

00:33:20.850 --> 00:33:23.230
It's attractive as an illness, don't you think?

00:33:23.790 --> 00:33:26.310
But its weak point is that it's not very contagious.

00:33:26.980 --> 00:33:30.080
You want to make it more contagious...

00:33:30.890 --> 00:33:34.070
and sell it as a biological weapon?

00:33:34.800 --> 00:33:38.370
Those guys supported me because that's what they thought.

00:33:38.370 --> 00:33:40.560
After all, they are weapons merchants.

00:33:40.560 --> 00:33:41.610
But...

00:33:42.160 --> 00:33:44.080
my goal is different.

00:33:45.010 --> 00:33:46.240
You plan on spreading it everywhere.

00:33:46.780 --> 00:33:47.740
That's correct.

00:33:54.690 --> 00:33:56.910
It will wipe out all of humanity.

00:33:57.620 --> 00:33:59.970
Only immortals like us will be left.

00:34:00.590 --> 00:34:02.540
We won't need to hide from the world anymore.

00:34:03.310 --> 00:34:07.770
Furthermore, I'll solve all the environmental and overpopulation problems.

00:34:08.700 --> 00:34:10.500
If you're thinking of eugenics...

00:34:11.450 --> 00:34:13.680
why don't you go live where there's no one else around?

00:34:14.780 --> 00:34:17.180
You still talk so spitefully.

00:34:24.090 --> 00:34:26.750
Do you know why I'm not wearing protective clothes?

00:34:28.140 --> 00:34:29.440
That's right.

00:34:29.440 --> 00:34:31.990
My plan has entered the final stage.

00:34:37.910 --> 00:34:41.300
I'll take you to your special seat.

00:34:41.300 --> 00:34:42.690
Before that...

00:34:42.690 --> 00:34:44.220
I'm going to silence you for a while.

00:35:22.400 --> 00:35:23.760
Sayara.

00:35:24.980 --> 00:35:27.040
That's Shibitojima.

00:35:28.520 --> 00:35:29.690
Wait a minute.

00:35:29.690 --> 00:35:31.030
That tanker...

00:35:31.850 --> 00:35:33.200
Go by that ship.

00:35:33.200 --> 00:35:33.730
Got it.

00:35:38.230 --> 00:35:38.940
Rin.

00:35:49.730 --> 00:35:50.490
Rin!

00:35:50.490 --> 00:35:51.210
Maeno.

00:35:51.800 --> 00:35:53.180
Hurry.

00:35:53.180 --> 00:35:54.100
Wait a minute.

00:35:54.100 --> 00:35:55.000
I'll get to it right away.

00:35:57.820 --> 00:35:59.340
A snow-making machine...

00:36:00.010 --> 00:36:02.350
I figured out where this ship is going.

00:36:02.350 --> 00:36:03.310
What did you say?

00:36:04.080 --> 00:36:04.850
Sorry.

00:36:04.850 --> 00:36:08.780
Snow-making machines work by spreading water vapor.

00:36:08.780 --> 00:36:11.710
She intends to use them to disperse the Higan virus in Tokyo.

00:36:12.000 --> 00:36:12.900
That's impossible.

00:36:13.230 --> 00:36:14.770
Why would she do something like that?

00:36:14.770 --> 00:36:16.850
Because she's Yamanobe Sayara.

00:36:17.950 --> 00:36:18.900
She's alive?

00:36:32.420 --> 00:36:33.240
Run away.

00:36:33.240 --> 00:36:34.240
Just a bit more.

00:36:35.020 --> 00:36:36.100
It's all right!

00:36:36.100 --> 00:36:36.790
There!

00:36:42.470 --> 00:36:43.050
No!

00:36:43.440 --> 00:36:44.120
Maeno.

00:36:44.120 --> 00:36:45.060
Maeno!

00:36:49.240 --> 00:36:50.190
Rin.

00:36:50.190 --> 00:36:51.290
Go.

00:36:51.790 --> 00:36:52.770
But...

00:36:53.690 --> 00:36:57.520
I'm... fine.

00:36:58.170 --> 00:36:59.320
Maeno...

00:37:02.680 --> 00:37:03.730
Wait.

00:37:26.870 --> 00:37:28.080
This is...

00:37:41.450 --> 00:37:44.390
You're the one who abducted Maeno's friend, aren't you?

00:37:44.390 --> 00:37:45.950
Who are you talking about?

00:37:45.950 --> 00:37:47.030
An ornithologist.

00:37:47.480 --> 00:37:48.860
Ah, him.

00:37:48.860 --> 00:37:50.660
That's right. That was me.

00:37:51.150 --> 00:37:53.500
I needed his knowledge for the plan.

00:37:54.150 --> 00:37:59.490
From Tokyo to Sanbanze, Wajiro, Australia, Thailand.

00:37:59.490 --> 00:38:01.450
Aren't those all bird nesting grounds?

00:38:01.870 --> 00:38:03.880
You're very knowledgeable.

00:38:03.880 --> 00:38:05.040
That's right.

00:38:05.040 --> 00:38:09.390
I thought about a scenario where they might try to quarantine themselves.

00:38:10.480 --> 00:38:13.480
No matter how much they try to isolate themselves from other outbreaks,

00:38:13.480 --> 00:38:15.360
they can never be saved.

00:38:15.360 --> 00:38:17.390
Migratory birds have no homes.

00:38:18.210 --> 00:38:20.540
You can watch from there.

00:38:20.540 --> 00:38:22.720
The sight of people dying en masse.

00:38:24.670 --> 00:38:24.970
What?

00:38:28.550 --> 00:38:29.500
Why?

00:38:34.110 --> 00:38:34.960
Why?

00:38:35.740 --> 00:38:36.670
An angel?

00:38:44.620 --> 00:38:46.250
Maeno?

00:38:47.070 --> 00:38:47.740
Shougo's?

00:38:51.970 --> 00:38:53.070
That's...

00:39:05.740 --> 00:39:06.770
Angel.

00:39:13.320 --> 00:39:16.100
Why did you do such a foolish thing?

00:39:16.100 --> 00:39:17.990
I'm sorry.

00:39:17.990 --> 00:39:22.280
But this is the only way I can protect you and my family.

00:39:23.500 --> 00:39:24.530
Kouki?

00:39:25.890 --> 00:39:28.990
Shougo-san was strong.

00:39:29.610 --> 00:39:32.220
To be able to suppress this desire.

00:39:38.910 --> 00:39:40.010
Rin.

00:39:40.010 --> 00:39:41.200
Thank you.

00:39:41.780 --> 00:39:45.020
I was really myself during these 20 years.

00:39:45.550 --> 00:39:48.680
You are... always...

00:39:48.680 --> 00:39:52.280
the real Maeno Kouki.

00:39:59.010 --> 00:40:00.460
Goodbye.

00:40:01.290 --> 00:40:03.070
While I am still myself.

00:40:11.810 --> 00:40:13.310
M-Maeno!

00:40:13.740 --> 00:40:15.290
Maeno!

00:40:20.830 --> 00:40:23.650
Eat me. Please.

00:40:23.650 --> 00:40:25.240
Eat me.

00:40:33.450 --> 00:40:34.770
This is great.

00:40:34.770 --> 00:40:36.310
This is the best.

00:40:47.780 --> 00:40:49.590
My, my.

00:40:49.590 --> 00:40:51.280
Hey, did you know?

00:40:52.200 --> 00:40:55.260
The only one who can eat the Fruit of Immortality...

00:40:55.710 --> 00:40:56.640
is me.

00:41:08.340 --> 00:41:10.980
No! Don't stop!

00:41:10.980 --> 00:41:14.520
A fruit that has the blood of two people.

00:41:14.520 --> 00:41:16.120
That's pretty rare.

00:41:23.330 --> 00:41:24.380
Damn.

00:41:24.380 --> 00:41:27.080
Please, don't go away.

00:41:27.610 --> 00:41:29.360
I'll have to make do with this.

00:41:37.670 --> 00:41:40.500
This one is more beautiful after all.

00:41:46.860 --> 00:41:47.730
It's no good.

00:41:47.730 --> 00:41:48.980
Still too young?

00:41:50.000 --> 00:41:52.720
I want to eat Rin's soon.

00:42:12.920 --> 00:42:15.570
Mimi, bring some water.

00:42:19.340 --> 00:42:20.340
Mimi?

00:42:34.580 --> 00:42:37.180
Hello. This is Asougi Consulting.

00:42:44.060 --> 00:42:45.540
No, um...

00:42:46.680 --> 00:42:50.280
Sorry, Maeno is currently on a trip.

00:42:52.390 --> 00:42:53.340
Yes.

